---
// OPTIONAL VISUAL 08 - why a smaller representation can matter.
//
// Deliberately hedged: "can potentially reduce" and "would have to be measured", because no
// measured savings exist in any of these categories yet. Neutral geometric icons only.
const AREAS = [
  { label: 'Storage', note: 'fewer bytes held at rest' },
  { label: 'Transfer', note: 'fewer bytes moved between systems' },
  { label: 'Handling', note: 'fewer bytes passed through processing steps' },
];
---

<figure class="ii" aria-labelledby="ii-caption">
  <ul class="ii-areas">
    {AREAS.map((area) => (
      <li class="ii-area">
        <span class="ii-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span>
        <span class="ii-label">{area.label}</span>
        <span class="ii-note">{area.note}</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <figcaption id="ii-caption" class="ii-caption">
    Reducing the representation of data can potentially reduce the infrastructure resources
    associated with storing or moving that representation. Whether it does, and by how much, would
    have to be measured for a given workload &mdash; ByteLite does not claim savings in any of
    these categories today.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
.ii { margin: 0; background: #0d1120; border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-radius: .875rem; padding: 1.75rem; }
.ii-areas { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: .875rem; }
@media (max-width: 640px) { .ii-areas { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
.ii-area {
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .3rem;
  background: #07090f; border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-radius: .5rem; padding: 1.125rem;
}
.ii-glyph { display: flex; gap: 3px; margin-bottom: .375rem; }
.ii-glyph span { width: .5rem; height: .875rem; border-radius: 1px; background: #2a3350; border: 1px solid #34406b; }
.ii-glyph span:first-child { background: rgba(99,102,241,.5); border-color: #6366f1; }
.ii-label { font-size: .9375rem; font-weight: 600; color: #e4e7f2; }
.ii-note { font-size: .8125rem; color: #7b829e; line-height: 1.5; }
.ii-caption {
  margin-top: 1.25rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid #1a2235;
  font-size: .875rem; color: #7b829e; line-height: 1.7;
}
@media (max-width: 600px) { .ii { padding: 1.25rem; } }
</style>
